. * FILTERS * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
. *** NOTE! In our PAP, we restricted the analysis of H3 to the years mentioned
>  below, since our reading of the SOEP data documentation suggested that these
>  would be the only years for which information about the chidrens' gender wou
> ld be available. However, in the actual data, these information are in princi
> ple avaiable in all years. Thus, we decided to run the analysis based on all 
> years for which the information are available. If desired, you can un-comment
>  the following line of code to restrict the analyses to those years that were
>  indicated in the PAP as supposedly being the only years in which these infor
> mation were available.
. *keep if syear==2001|syear==2006|syear==2011|syear==2016
. 
. 
. *** Only include married people living together (married, i.e., exclude marri
> ed, but separated (2), singles, divorced, widowed, partner living abroad). Ot
> her than indicated in the PAP, individuals in civil union are not counted her
> e because, as we explained in the PAP, we only include partners of different 
> genders (which contradicts including individuals in civil union)
. keep if pgfamstd >=0
(2,315 observations deleted)

. gen live_together = 1 if pgfamstd==1
(357,250 missing values generated)

. replace live_together = 0 if live_together==.
(357,250 real changes made)

. keep if live_together == 1
(357,250 observations deleted)

. 
. 
. * GENERATE VARIABLES * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
. *** Generate treatment variable: Has exactly one child, and that child is fem
> ale
. *** Note: We use sumkids and daughter instead of pld0025 and bgp15307a (which
>  we mentioned in our PAP), since these variables did not contain the desired 
> information for all necessary years
. keep if sumkids==1
(240,996 observations deleted)

. gen d_daughter=1 if kidsex01==2
(32,253 missing values generated)

. replace d_daughter = 0 if d_daughter==.
